   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT relating to permitting the Setauket fire district and Stony Brook fire\ndistrict to enter into contracts with the state university of New York at\nStony Brook for property, services, and other consideration",
    "basePrintNo": "S7889",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7889-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7889\n\nSPONSOR: PALUMBO\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to permitting the Setauket fire district and Stony Brook\nfire district to enter into contracts with the state university of New\nYork at Stony Brook for property, services, and other consideration\n\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act relating to permitting the Setauket fire district and Stony Brook\nfire district to enter into contracts with the state university of New\nYork at Stony Brook for property, services, and other consideration\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo make it easier for the Setauket Fire District and the Stony Brook\nFire District to contract with the State University of New York at Stony\nBrook for the provision of property and services.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection I. Authorizes the Setauket Fire District and the Stony Brook\nFire District to enter into agreements or contracts with the Sta te\nUniversity of New York at Stony Brook related to the provision of emer-\ngency medical services or fire protection and for the recipr ocal\nprovision of services and other considerations of equivalent value.\n\nSection 2. Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe State University of New York at Stony Brook has expressed a mutual\nwillingness to contract with the Setauket and Stony Brook fire districts\nfor the provision of equipment and services. Under current law, it is\ndifficult for the two parties to contract with one a nother. This bill\nseeks to make the process less complicated and encourage future cooper-\nation between the respective parties.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThe first of January next succeeding the date on which it shall have\nbecome a law.\n",
